  "period_note": "Year-end position from the Annual Report's own multi-year '5 Years' Financial Summary' table (audited, Solo/Stand Alone basis; cross-validated against the same report's separate 'Horizontal Analysis (Stand Alone)' Balance Sheet and Profit & Loss tables, which reproduce Total assets/liabilities/equity and the full P&L exactly). FY2024 was UCB's sector-wide asset-quality recognition event: NPL jumped from 5.50% (FY2023) to 14.90%, Total Provision (excl. tax) nearly tripled from BDT 4,548mn to 12,933mn, and specific-provision coverage of NPL fell from 49.99% to 26.18% (22,341/85,344) even as absolute specific provisions rose. Net profit after tax collapsed from BDT 2,685mn to BDT 608mn and ROE fell to a new series low of 1.44%. Capital adequacy moved into shortfall for the first time in the series: CAR fell from 12.58% to 10.59% against a required capital of BDT 63,587.78mn versus actual Total Capital of BDT 53,859mn, i.e. a reported Capital Surplus/(Shortage) of BDT (9,728.77)mn (verified: 53,859 - 63,587.78 = -9,728.78, reconciling to the reported -9,728.77 to a rounding cent). Authorized capital was raised from BDT 15,000mn to BDT 25,000mn during the year. DISCREPANCY vs already-stored FY2023 data: this report's FY2023 comparative column shows Net asset value per share restated to BDT 28.30, vs BDT 29.68 in FY2023's own contemporaneous annual report (ucb-annual-report-2023.txt) already stored in 2023_Q4.json. Per project convention the earlier (contemporaneous) 29.68 is kept unchanged in 2023_Q4.json; this restatement is recorded here and in sources.json only. All other FY2020-FY2023 comparative figures in this table (interest income/expense, NII, non-interest income/expenses, operating profit, PBT, PAT, authorized/paid-up capital, equity, deposits, loans, investments, fixed assets, total assets/liabilities, RWA, Tier I/II capital and ratios, CAR, NPL amount/%, provisions, EPS-as-reported, market price, ROA, ROE, cost-to-income, credit-deposit ratio) reproduce exactly against the previously stored 2020_Q4-2023_Q4.json files with zero divergence.",
